## Quick start

Load the client into your workspace with [Link](https://dyalog.github.io/link/):

```apl
]LINK.Create # ./APLSource
```

Then create a client:

```apl
config ← (
    baseUrl: '{{ base_url ?? "https://your-api-server.com" }}'
{{~ if has_security_schemes ~}}
    security: (
{{~ for scheme in security_schemes ~}}
{{~ if scheme.value.type == "apikey" ~}}
        apiKey: {{ if scheme.value.in == "header" }}'env:[API_KEY]'  {{ else }}'your-api-key'   {{ end }}         ⍝ {{ scheme.value.name }}
{{~ else if scheme.value.type == "http" && scheme.value.scheme == "bearer" ~}}
        bearerToken: 'env:[API_TOKEN]'    ⍝ {{ scheme.value.name }}
{{~ else if scheme.value.type == "http" && scheme.value.scheme == "basic" ~}}
        username: 'username'              ⍝ {{ scheme.value.name }}
        password: 'password'
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
    )
{{~ end ~}}
)
client ← ⎕NEW {{ class_name ?? "Client" }} config
```
{{~ if tag_docs.size > 0 ~}}

Each operation is a function in a namespace named after its tag, and takes a namespace of
arguments. For example:

```apl
{{ tag_docs[0].operations[0].usage_example }}
response.HttpStatus    ⍝ e.g. 200
response.Data          ⍝ the response body, parsed from JSON
```

The result is an [HttpCommand response](https://dyalog.github.io/HttpCommand/latest/result-response/).
HTTP errors do not signal an APL error, so check `response.HttpStatus` (or `response.IsOK`).
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if has_security_schemes ~}}

## Authentication
{{~ for scheme in security_schemes ~}}

### {{ scheme.value.name }}

{{~ if scheme.value.type == "apikey" ~}}
An API key, sent in the `{{ scheme.value.parameter_name }}` {{ if scheme.value.in == "query" }}query parameter{{ else }}{{ scheme.value.in }}{{ end }}{{ if scheme.value.in == "cookie" }} (cookie API keys are not yet supported by the generated client){{ end }}. Set `security.apiKey` in the config.
{{~ else if scheme.value.type == "http" && scheme.value.scheme == "bearer" ~}}
A bearer token{{ if scheme.value.bearer_format }} ({{ scheme.value.bearer_format }}){{ end }}, sent in the `Authorization` header. Set `security.bearerToken` in the config.
{{~ else if scheme.value.type == "http" && scheme.value.scheme == "basic" ~}}
HTTP basic authentication. Set `security.username` and `security.password` in the config.
{{~ else ~}}
Type `{{ scheme.value.type }}`{{ if scheme.value.scheme }}, scheme `{{ scheme.value.scheme }}`{{ end }}. This scheme is not yet supported by the generated client.
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if scheme.value.description ~}}

{{ scheme.value.description }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}

A credential sent in a header (a bearer token, or an API key in a header) can be given as `env:[NAME]`,
to read it from the environment variable `NAME` when a request is sent.
{{~ end ~}}
